**Summary:**
- Extracted ResumeBanner + ResumableRunBanner JSX (~600 lines) and the `/api/courses/active-run` probe out of `src/app/create/page.tsx` into a new shared client module `src/components/ResumeGenerationBanner.tsx` exposing `useResumeRunData()` hook + `ResumeGenerationBanners` orchestrator + the underlying banner components. Same testids, same network calls, same UX.
- Mounted `<ResumeGenerationBanners sticky={false} onNavigateToGeneration={(slug) => router.push('/create?resume=…')} />` on `src/app/page.tsx` above the sticky header. `sticky={false}` lets it scroll with content rather than fighting the home page's existing sticky header.
- The host returns `null` (no wrapper) when there's no active/paused run — verified `wrapperBefore == 0` in Playwright when nothing is generating (the "zero extra container" AC). When something IS running it wraps in `<div data-testid="resume-generation-banners" style="display: contents">` which is invisible to layout.
- 5 new unit tests pass; full suite shows only the pre-existing 21 failures from US-191/US-194 (untouched).
- Browser-verified end-to-end: clean home (0 banners), start a real mock run, reload home → banner appears with name + Resume + Cancel-and-restart, click Resume → navigates to `/create?resume=<slug>` and Stage 6 panel mounts.
